ery draw: FY2027 total revenue (judge neutral by consensus lookup; gold $400–435 billion) and Vera CPU revenue (judge takes management's $20 billion at face value; gold $8–18 billion); never judged: NVIDIA's own capex in every draw, the operating margin in two (evidence never reached them). Alex then set the terms (D263): the gold is Claude's standard, a disagreement is a gap to close in the judge, not a verdict; `judging-v7` (`poc-v91`) writes reader B's five behaviours into the judge (guided growth carried forward, targets for unshipped products discounted by default, unsized commitments sized from their comparable, figures derived from accounting identities, consistency with linked conclusions); on the stored requests of the seven questions that differed, six now land in the gold's band (`proof-judging-v7.txt`). The end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`: Alex's call. At Alex's word the frozen ruler is written as a whole in AGENTS §7.1 ("The frozen ruler": the extraction standard and golden-v5, the seeds, the judgement ruler, with their sha256) with pointers in §1, §5, §7.3, §8 and the closing checklist, in both worktrees' AGENTS.md; `tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` fails the suite when any frozen file's hash moves. The acceptance run of poc-v91 (three draws at once, `arms/r5-accept-v91/`) was launched at 17:24 and stopped at Alex's word at 17:27 inside its first day (about five cents, no result); he then asked for the run settings to be written into AGENTS first (§9, "Run settings and where the time goes": judgements 32 at a time, extraction 16, Jev 8, call timeout 180 s, three draws at once, the serial chain at the item's turn) and said not to run again: there is an architecture problem to settle first (his words, quoted in AGENTS §9 and the work plan). That evening he asked why the open library was never adopted as the extraction's context and, given the traced answer (his 10-31 instruction framed as an experiment, the one-draw v82 replay judged "not adopted" by me, the D256 proposal left waiting), chose the architecture (D264, his words there): the extraction reads the day's open questions and their takes lines and decides the filing itself, on the latest extraction prompt. Built the same evening as extraction v72 / `poc-v92` (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v72.md`: role-v66's text with one paragraph pointing at [Open questions] and the links field, the takes lines written by `placement.question_lines` for both requests, the links field defined by `placement.FILING_RULE`, no placement call, a statement linked to nothing dropped as 'no home'; two snapshot wirings fixed: the seeds visible on the first day, the takes lines frozen within the day), proved at $0 (four new tests, each killed by its mutant; 274 pass; preflight over arm 4 draw 1) and for cents on the four rack-delay articles (`proof-v72-links.txt`: the statements that name nothing go to the Rubin Ultra / Kyber seed in 3/3 sends of three articles, once to the revenue sink in the fourth; zero candidates where the control proposed four Kyber duplicates), then launched at 18:05 as six draws, `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` against `arms/r6-control-v91/d1..3`, predictions frozen (`predictions-v72.sha256`). Scored at 19:40 on the frozen ruler (`e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`, `log.md` row 12, `design-v72.md` §8, D264): v92 against v91, three-draw means, core reaching 76.3 → 73.7 of 86, core dropped for no home 4.0 → 5.7, supporting reaching 94.0 → 90.0, noise reaching 89.2 → 56.9, article-opened questions 11.7 → 3.0 (must_open 28/28 and may_open 40/42 in both, covered by the seeds), judgement agreement 17/19, 17/18, 17/19 → 15/18, 16/17, 17/18, cost $1.15 → $0.88 a draw, model time −36%, no re-sent request. Neither better nor worse on the desk's counts, cleaner and cheaper; not the default. Two mechanisms traced, both sentences: the revenue sink (60–62% of links on the three company-wide revenue questions against 34–40%; the model's account names D259's figure-line clause and concedes the narrowest-only rule) and role-v66's end check removing 21 supporting matters a draw that v53 keeps (`matter-states-r6-v72.txt`). Alex then fixed the version (D265: v72 / poc-v92 is the latest version and the default, no drift; experiment the next steps on it), and two fixes were built directly, no arm (`log.md` row 13, `design-v72.md` §9): (a) `extraction.narrowest_links`, code under every configuration, a statement under a driver and its root keeps the driver, replayed over the three v92 ledgers at $0 (links −31–34%, the three revenue questions' share 60–62% → 42–45%, no statement left without a home); (b) `review-v73` / `poc-v93`, the closing check's three example-less boundaries given their kept-side example, proved for cents on the 17 articles of the 20 lost supporting matters (present 10 → 28 of 60 sends, the probed cases 0/3, 1/3, 0/3 → 2/3, 3/3, 3/3; the noise guard on the same articles 0.47 → 0.61 statements per article per send). **The one next task:** three draws of poc-v93 against the v92 baseline on the frozen ruler (about $2.7), at Alex's word; then the next classes in order: the noise filed under the Data Center revenue question (the extraction's keep rule, standard 5.1 item 5 and 5.3; count the 52 gold not-kept statements a draw by mechanism first), the candidates the shown list suppresses (65 → 6.7 a draw; no loss on this window's ruler because the seeds cover must_open 28/28, a risk elsewhere), the judge's daily rung churn (60–74% of later judgements move the rung; count per question), the quote check's refusals of core statements. The work plan's step 0 is thereby the control of this comparison; the rest of `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/workplan-2026-11-02.md` stands (then the extraction noise class, the D2 right-question mapping as a new ruler piece, the never-judged questions, identity R2-d/R2-g, judge consistency, a second acceptance run). Next, one at a time by the same method: (1) the extraction's noise is now the largest visible class (gold not-kept and unlisted statements written, 105 and 107 a draw; the standard's 5.1 item 5 and 5.3 own it): count it by mechanism on the stored answers before any prompt change; (2) the D3 stance gold: readers who did not write the code judge, for a sample of judgements, whether the stated reference and implied outcome follow from the evidence shown and whether the rung follows them (the ladder's neutral band naming its comparator at opening, PRD 06 ladder rule 2, is the extraction's open rule); (3) the identity class keeps R2-d (GAAP basis, growth against level) and R2-g (the names of one research group deciding launch/shipment pairs) open; (4) a whole-pipeline run on the new code and `poc-v90` is Alex's call, not a next arm. A letter-suffixed prompt version keeps its number's behaviour and reads its own files (`extraction.version_number`, test `test_prompt_version_suffix.py`); `role-v53b` exists and is byte-identical to `role-v53`. The census of arm 2 (`dropped-census-r2-placement-v3.md`) puts the placement step's own share of the loss at 11 of 25 dropped core matters and 11 of 107 supporting; the rest have no fitting open question (by design under D209/D248, or the opening step's). Two calls for Alex came out of it (`plan.md` §5 (e), (f)): whether D207's "company's own only" rule gives way to the takes line's gate, and whether the extraction's one-line summary must name the matter a statement belongs to (one story, the Rubin Ultra rack delay, lost 6–7 core matters because its statements say "NVL72x2" or "back-to-back racks" and the question says "Rubin Ultra / Kyber"; the placer reads statements, not articles). The measuring stick was checked on the way: 78 of the 80 core matters an extraction reached are strict sentence matches, 2 word-overlap matches both read as the same matter; the proof harness `harness/resend_place_set.py` now counts only statements of matters that reached no question.

**Alex's calls first, three of them (2026-10-31 evening; `research/2026-10-31-reference-context/`).** The end-to-end measurement over the first 14 days of July (118 gold articles, three draws per arm, `e2e_compare.py`) settled the architecture question of the morning: the extraction that reads the open questions (extraction v71, `poc-v82`) was not adopted (noise reaching judgement up, core unchanged, fewer questions; `design-v71-production.md`), and the bottleneck is placement, which drops a third of the core matters for want of a question to file them under. Two steps were then built and measured against the same control: (1) seed questions (D253, D208 step one: `seeding.py`, `scripts/replay.py --seed`, `poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01.json`): core matters dropped 30.0 → 26.3 per draw, must-open 28/28; (2) the placement prompt `placement-narrow-v2` (`poc-v83`, two Codex audits): core dropped 26.3 → 21.3, supporting 96.3 → 89.7, link precision blind 29/40 → 34/40, noise and the figure questions' share of links unchanged (`design-placement-v2.md`, measured section). Reading the 22 core matters still dropped: 10–14 had no fitting question shown (the ten hand-written seeds lack EPS, China revenue and share, the revenue-sharing programme as a deal, 2028 AI capex, and Kyber before day 6), 7 had one shown and the placer answered none, 1 fell to the extraction's quote check. The deep review of the method that followed (`review-2026-10-31-method.md`) re-estimated the ruler (noise reaching judgement is about 22 a draw in both arms, between 17 and 26 by two blind readers of the pieces that reach, not the 20 first reported; 16–18 of the 28–30 questions a draw opens are blind-judged duplicates of one bet, half of them of a seed; about 12% of the core and supporting pieces that reach sit under a wrong question; two of the ten seeds were written with knowledge of the window's news, worth about one core matter a draw) and refuted one lean with a stored re-send: stripping the takes line's "direct drivers … with a size" clause removed no noise and cost 11 core or supporting homes. The noise that reaches is seven tenths under the credit-support programme's questions, routed there by D207's "names that matter" rule; only the extraction can stop it (D252's paired examples, role-v65, measured at the extraction layer only). The calls: (a) make `placement-narrow-v2` the placement prompt, with its clause "when the question's market and period cover them" cut (the placer's own account names it for dropping a core share statement; D240's principle); (b) generate the seeds from `poc/universe.json`'s watch list by code and have the analyst add the driver questions the list lacks (EPS root, competition and share including China, the programme as a deal question), Alex signing the list before anyone reads the window's articles; (c) the order R1 seeds → R2 D248 items 2–3 in matching identity → R3 role-v65 end to end, each with a $0 proof on stored requests first. Done on his word to start the work (2026-10-31 night, loop log row 69): R1's second seed file (`poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json`, 23 questions with provenance, `design-seed-v2.md` with the $0 proof and frozen predictions) and its three replays, which stopped on day 1 with Jev HTTP 402 (the account's credit; only Alex restores it; the folders `poc/data/e2e-v83-seedv2-d1..3` resume with their run.sh); R2's census, design, $0 replay and code on branch `fix/question-identity-r2` (worktree `hivemind-identity-r2`; `design-r2-identity.md` §5), measured after R1. R3's first step (2026-11-01, loop log rows 70–71, `design-r3-review.md`): of the ten core or supporting statements that reach judgement under role-v53 and role-v65's stored draws keep in at most one, the model's own account traced one to a rule, the closing check's views row ("a quote that only characterises") dropping a company's denial of a reported delay; role-v66 (`poc-v84`; role and categories identical to v65, `review-v66.txt` adds one boundary to that row, the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands is judged as the plan itself would be; two Codex audits; `extraction.REVIEW_UNTIL` 65 → 66) was sent on the whole bench, three draws against the stored v65 draws: the denial 1/3 → 3/3 and an unseen denial of the same kind 0/3 → 2/3, none of the 17 guard noise statements re-admitted in two draws, core every draw 72 → 70 and supporting 122 → 120 inside the two-send noise floor, gold-rejected kept 59.3 → 60.7; the per-statement flips (22 new, 17 gone) are at the scale of two sends of one prompt (8 and 21). R3's end-to-end arm therefore uses role-v66 in place of v65, after R1 and R2, and needs Jev credit. Open for Alex: R2-c (the collision judge no longer overrides a code identity) and R2-d (figure-question duplicates: one plan's wordings, growth against level, GAAP against non-GAAP). The default stays role-v53 / `poc-v69` (placement v1, no seeds) until he decides; a switch names its `poc` config in `scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test and the README, and is recorded. After these: D248 items 2–3 in matching identity (11 of 30 questions a draw opens are one bet under another deadline or milestone), then the record-field class (F1–F8) and opening (O1–O9).

The handoff plan with every open task, the principles and the quantitative criteria is [`handoff-plan-2026-10-30.md`](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/handoff-plan-2026-10-30.md).

**Evidence bloat, before anything else downstream:** not solved, reduced at the source. The window rule (D198, judging-v5) hides old pieces by recency, not by count: in the sealed three-month ledger the largest judging request after it (Data Center revenue) still showed 647 pieces (1,185 hidden), 93,634 input tokens, because a broad thesis took 40–60 new links a day. Placement under the one-home rule (D207–D209) cut the first week's links per item 3.3 → 1.82 and the largest thesis's links 106 → 52, the largest judging request 15,229 → 8,649 tokens (`english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28` against the sealed ledger's same week), measured over one week with role-v22 only. The decisive test is the whole-pipeline run over the three-month window with `poc-v69` (on Alex's go, with a cap), read for links per thesis, the largest judging request and any halt; the structural answer, a versioned argument record per question for the judge to read, is designed nowhere yet (handoff plan T6).

## Parallel day (D172–D183)

The replay runs the parallel day by default (D183: Alex chose it to converge faster); `scripts/replay.py --workers 1` runs the serial path, needed to resume a day a serial run left unfinished. Measured live on the complete July 27 day (53 items), three serial against three parallel trials interleaved ([result](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/results.md)): median 501.8 s → 112.5 s, **4.46× end to end**, 5.91× for item work; daily judging (~37–40 s) is the same code in both modes. Every trial's audit is clean; each parallel trial's runner accepted exactly the rebuilt exact-prefix request for all 53 items; each trial's answers replayed through the other mode give an identical ledger. Drift from the recorded sequential golden is inside the serial trials' own spread. The product entry point (`--workers 16`) ran the same day live in 135.5 s with the same checks clean. On recorded answers the parallel day equals the golden in all ten tables (D180, and again on the promoted module).

Fifteen consecutive days (August 1–15, 221 items) with every call answered by one deterministic oracle of the request bytes, at no cost (D182, [result](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-multi-day-oracle/results.md)): the parallel ledger equals the serial one in all 20 product tables, its turns accepted exactly the serial run's 221 extraction requests, and a broken runner was caught. At recorded call durations the fifteen days take an estimated 2.79× less time (2,512 s → 900 s); a busy day gains 3.6–4.5×, a day of a few items 1.5–2×.

What remains of the time is not scheduling: items that depend on the item just before them (~45–60 s), daily judging (D63), and each item's two matching phases in order (~17 s). Ten times end to end on this day would need those to shrink.

