   Two corrections matter:

   - v74i’s **17-item answer misses the opening market judgement**; its 16-item answer includes it.
   - v74h’s **4-item answer includes that judgement**. v74i’s 6-item answer reaches SharonAI and Firmus near the article’s end, so it did not simply stop reading halfway.

   These are separate problems: skipping whole subjects, and inconsistently accepting individual statements. More items alone will not fix both. See the raw answers in [v108, core-noise](sends-placeholder) and [v107, core-noise](sends-placeholder-2), under `answers["gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6"]`. The recorded v108 result independently confirms the opening claim appears only once: [proof-v108-a-mixed11.txt:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-a-mixed11.txt:37).

2. **The output budget can bind, but the available production records strongly argue against it here.**

   `max_output_tokens` becomes OpenAI’s `max_completion_tokens`, which includes reasoning and visible output: [model.py:110](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/model.py:110), [official API definition](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat/subresources/completions/methods/create).

   I queried all extraction calls in `arms/r7-combined-v94/d{1,2,3}/archive.sqlite`:

   | Trinity call | Evidence items | Completion tokens, including reasoning | Reasoning tokens | Finish |
   |---|---:|---:|---:|---|
   | d1, call 200 | 9 | 2,286 | 614 | stop |
   | d2, call 212 | 7 | 1,842 | 776 | stop |
   | d3, call 208 | 7 | 1,882 | 690 | stop |

   All three had an **8,000-token limit**. Across **729 extraction calls**, every finish was `stop`; the largest completion was **2,942 tokens**.

   **Limitation:** these are v74 production calls, not v74i. The later resend harness discards everything except parsed answer content, so its saved answers cannot establish their finish reasons or reasoning usage: [resend_targets.py:70](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/resend_targets.py:70). Production preserves both in `response_json`: [model.py:233](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/model.py:233).

3. **Length alone does not explain the instability; the request permits an incomplete walk to look complete.**

   I counted every answer in the 23 matching saved files: **1,086 sends, 362 three-send groups, 46 distinct articles**. The usual “50 articles” comprises overlapping selections; v102 has only five selected articles.

   | Article length, characters | Distinct articles | Sends | Mean items/send | Mean three-send count range |
   |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   | <5,000 | 27 | 603 | 3.48 | 1.57 |
   | 5,000–9,999 | 15 | 351 | 4.48 | 2.06 |
   | 10,000–19,999 | 2 | 63 | 2.25 | 1.90 |
   | ≥20,000 | 2 | 69 | 7.49 | 5.04 |

   Pearson correlation between length and count spread is **0.46**, but **0.12 excluding Trinity**. Length versus written count similarly falls from **0.30 to −0.05**. This selected sample does not establish a general long-item effect. A shorter T8 article, *DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow*, produces **[3,12,7]** at 6,418 characters.

   The relevant request sentences are:

   - “**Go through the item from its first paragraph to its last**” and “**not a selection**”: the intended behaviour is already explicit. [role-v74i.txt:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:5)
   - “**Read each evidence item back**”: the closing check examines what was written, without explicitly revisiting omitted source passages. [review-v74i.txt:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/review-v74i.txt:1)
   - T8 requests “**forecasts, estimates, calculations and specific judgements**,” but excludes “**general arguments or risk lists**.” That distinction is a plausible source of inconsistent treatment of the opening judgement, **not a proven cause**. [categories-v74i.json:33](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v74i.json:33)

   Rebuilding the request from d1 shows **22 questions**, including revenue questions and capex questions—not just v9. Its v9 line names “**financing commitments and capacity backstops to customers and partners**,” closely matching the article’s dominant topic. But the role explicitly says a takes line “**never [says] that a statement is material**.” Topic anchoring is therefore a plausible model failure, not an instruction to select one topic. [role-v74i.txt:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:1), [placement.py:53](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/placement.py:53)

