4. **My preferred structural candidate is a coarse section-by-section check inside the same call, while retaining one final evidence list.**

   These are expected effects, not measured improvements:

   | Priority | Option | Completeness and noise | Cost and possible breakage |
   |---|---|---|---|
   | **1** | Code assigns source-section IDs; the final check revisits every section for missing qualifying statements | Directly addresses unchecked omissions. Allow zero evidence per section; no quotas or compulsory paragraph facts | Modest extra output and reasoning. The model may falsely mark a section complete; code verifies coverage bookkeeping, not semantic completeness |
   | **2** | Raise reasoning from low to medium | May improve whole-request execution and difficult keep/reject distinctions; no completeness guarantee | More tokens and latency; could over-filter or reach the shared output cap. Test before applying to all T8 items or choosing a length threshold |
   | **3** | Put the article before the question list | Cheap test of topic anchoring; unchanged materiality rules | Little token change; may weaken filing accuracy or merely move attention elsewhere |
   | **4** | Raise output limit alone | Helps actual capped responses; little supporting evidence here | A higher ceiling need not increase usage, but permits greater spend. Does not require fuller reading |

   **Separate section calls have potentially strong coverage benefits, but are not my recommended next step.** They repeat the prompt and questions, lose cross-section context, and complicate deduplication. Exact duplicates could merge by **original article ID plus original source span**; sharing v9, similar wording, or equal numbers is insufficient. Different spans describing the same matter still require semantic reconciliation. Otherwise splitting inflates the evidence count. It also conflicts with D199’s standing one-call decision: [DECISIONS.md:2569](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2569).

   The v17 warning is concrete: paragraph accounting improved overlap but tripled evidence volume and roughly doubled extraction/matching cost. It even exhausted an 8,000-token budget on reasoning once. Therefore **do not restore mandatory evidence-or-skip accounts for every paragraph**. [single-call/log.md:230](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md:230)

5. **Cheapest useful test of the top candidate: 18 calls, with everything else fixed.**

   Use three articles, **three unchanged sends plus three section-check sends each**:

   - **Trinity:** the observed multi-subject omission.
   - **DeepSeek … Major Blow:** the shorter unstable T8 counterexample.
   - **How Nvidia Became the Black Sheep …:** a steadier T8 control, currently **[9,9,10]**.

   Preserve full source text, question snapshot, schema field order, materiality rules, model, effort and budget. Save full responses, including finish reason and usage. Compare existing gold matters recovered **in every send**, core and supporting separately, plus rejected material admitted and cost. Read the actual missing passages; **a larger or steadier count is not success**.

   No files changed and no paid calls made.


